language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Joe's account number x has all the digits from 0 to 9 in some order; in each of the given sets exactly num_correct_digits digits are in their correct position.
given num_correct_digits : int(0..10)
$ the four sets Joe tried, each a list of the ten digits
given sets : matrix indexed by [int(1..4), int(1..10)] of int(0..9)
$ the digits of Joe's account number, by position
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..10)] of int(0..9)

branching on [x]
such that
$ the account number has every digit from 0 to 9 exactly once
allDiff(x),
$ in each set, exactly num_correct_digits digits are in their correct position
forAll k : int(1..4) . ((sum i : int(1..10) . toInt(sets[k, i] = x[i])) = num_correct_digits)
